# Root build context — used by `deploy/Dockerfile.edge`, which needs both
# `frontend/` and `deploy/Caddyfile` and so cannot use a narrower context.
#
# `backend/.dockerignore` covers the backend image separately; this file must
# stand on its own because Docker reads only the one belonging to the context
# in use.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.git
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Nothing in the image is built from these, and they are the bulk of the tree.
research/
prompts/
docs/
assets/
tools/
**/*.md
!deploy/**/*.md

# Local state and editor noise.
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/coverage
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/caddy_data
**/caddy_config
